# harness/tools/gates.manifest -- ONE HOME for how each gate artifact is built (CLAUDE.md 2F).
#
# ★★★★ WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The four gate probes were built with four DIFFERENT flag sets, and
# that fact lived in four different places (res_run.ps1, vm_run.ps1, build_comp.sh, and for pic
# and cel: NOWHERE AT ALL). Recovering pic's and cel's flags took a brute-force size-match against
# the shipped artifact, because no file in the tree recorded them. **A build line that exists only
# in a shell history is the L-45 defect applied to the assemble step** -- run_gates.sh already
# fixed it for the LAUNCH step and left the BUILD step exactly as it was.
#
# ★★★ It is also what lets gate_audit.py PROVE staleness instead of inferring it. An mtime says
# "the source tree moved"; it does not say the artifact is wrong. pic_probe.bin was a full day
# stale by mtime and byte-identical to a fresh build -- the renderer gate's 45/45 was never
# invalidated. With the flags recorded here the audit can rebuild and COMPARE BYTES, which is
# the question that actually matters.
#
# format:  name <TAB> source <TAB> artifact <TAB> flags (space-separated, may be empty)
# ★ Flags are load-bearing: comp built with -DHAL_GFX_MODE_SERVICE is 1,373 bytes, not 967, and
# is a different program from the one the compositing numbers were established against.
# ★★★★★ AD-96: THE pic GATE HAS FOUR CONFIGURATIONS AND THIS FILE RECORDED ONE.
# The `pic` row builds the artifact the 45/45 CORRECTNESS gate runs -- unpacked, counters in,
# 2,642 B, median 5.9349 s. **Every published room-render TIMING figure comes from a different
# program**: 2.746 s is -DPIC_NOCOUNT unpacked (2,512 B) and 2.832 s is -DPIC_NOCOUNT -DPRI_PACKED
# (2,971 B). Both were reproduced to the millisecond at T-P0-041, so neither figure is wrong --
# **they simply describe binaries this manifest did not build.**
# ★★★★ WHICH FIGURE IS CURRENT FOR THE ROOM RENDER: **2.832 s**, the packed nocount build.
# Packing is load-bearing (P3b.3: without it the draw phase does not integrate), so the packed
# configuration is the one the design plans against; the unpacked 2.746 s is its control, and the
# counted 5.9349 s is the correctness gate and is NOT a performance figure -- counters cost 2.16x.
# ★★★ The timing rows are marked `timing` in column 5 so a reader cannot take a median from a row
# built for correctness, which is exactly the substitution AD-96 records.
pic	src/harness/pic_probe.s	build/pic_probe.bin	-DHAL_GFX_MODE_SERVICE	correctness 45/45, median 5.9349 s (counters in -- not a perf figure)	purpose=correctness
pic_nc	src/harness/pic_probe.s	build/pic_nc_unpacked.bin	-DHAL_GFX_MODE_SERVICE -DPIC_NOCOUNT	timing 2.7456 s median (unpacked control)	purpose=timing
pic_nc_pk	src/harness/pic_probe.s	build/pic_nc_packed.bin	-DHAL_GFX_MODE_SERVICE -DPIC_NOCOUNT -DPRI_PACKED	timing 2.8319 s median -- ★ THE CURRENT ROOM-RENDER FIGURE	purpose=timing
pic_win	src/harness/pic_probe.s	build/pic_v_windowed_nocount.bin	-DHAL_GFX_MODE_SERVICE -DPLANE_WINDOWED -DPIC_NOCOUNT	timing 2.9204 s median (+6.4%, windowed per-pixel class)	purpose=timing
res	src/harness/res_probe.s	build/res_probe.bin	-DHAL_GFX_MODE_SERVICE	purpose=correctness
cel	src/harness/cel_probe.s	build/cel_probe.bin	-DHAL_GFX_MODE_SERVICE -DHAL_SYS_FAST_CLOCK	purpose=correctness
comp	src/harness/comp_probe.s	build/comp_probe.bin	purpose=correctness
vm	src/harness/vm_probe.s	build/vm_probe.bin	-DHAL_GFX_MODE_SERVICE -DHAL_SYS_FAST_CLOCK	purpose=correctness
# ★★★★★ AD-140 SAID THE `vm` ROW IS purpose=correctness WHILE THE HEADLINE VM TIMING FIGURE COMES
# FROM IT. The premise is right and FLIPPING THE ROW WOULD BE WRONG: the 9/9 state diff genuinely
# is a correctness gate, and flag_diff.py deliberately exempts those from EXPECTED_ON because "the
# clock cannot change a byte and the counters cannot" (line 121). Flipping it would raise a false
# alarm on the gate and still not describe the timing build.
# ★★★★ THE DEFECT IS A MISSING ROW, NOT A WRONG FIELD. The timing figure comes from a DIFFERENT
# build of the same source -- the VM_TIMED free-run, which the manifest did not list at all, so
# HAL_SYS_FAST_CLOCK was never asserted for it. That is exactly the absence AD-100 cost a task to.
# ★★★ VM_NOCOUNT is deliberately NOT expected-on here: it is measured at 1.44% [P3b.2] and 3.40%
# [P4.6], which is the ablation class, not PIC_NOCOUNT's 2.16x "your figure is not comparable"
# class. ★★ A P6.10 figure quoted from this row therefore carries counters, and carries a stated
# 1.4-3.4% instrumentation share rather than a silent one.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ★★★★★ THIS ROW'S FIGURES ARE RETIRED AT T-P0-084h, AND THE PRODUCER IS WHY.
#     retired:  67.802 ms/cycle room 83 (0 obj), 113.495 room 1 (4 obj)   [P6.10]
#     producer: vm_probe.bin 9,660 B EC8991A5...  ->  9,667 B 771F147D...
# ★★★★ Route (b) put the LOGIC decode at vm_bind_logic in vm_run.s, which vm_probe.s links -- so
# the binary moved by 7 bytes AND the VM now does work it did not do before: a fresh LOGIC bind
# decrypts its message strings. **The old medians describe a VM that never decoded.** Leaving them
# here live would be AD-96 exactly -- a figure whose producer has changed -- and this arc has
# already walked into that once.
# ★★★ NOT RE-MEASURED, AND SAYING SO RATHER THAN GUESSING. A VM_TIMED free-run publishes no
# per-cycle trace, so vm_run.ps1's diff reports FAIL on it; reading a median needs a driver path
# T-P0-084h did not work out. **A retired figure with a named retiring task beats a fresh figure
# nobody can reproduce** [L-45's shape applied to a measurement].
# ★★ The `vm` row above is unaffected in MEANING: it is purpose=correctness and survives on its 9/9
# state diff, which was re-run on the new binary and is byte-identical on every compared cycle for
# all nine titles.
vm_timed	src/harness/vm_probe.s	build/vm_probe.bin	-DHAL_GFX_MODE_SERVICE -DHAL_SYS_FAST_CLOCK	VM_TIMED=N free-run; binary 771F147D 9,667 B; P6.10's medians RETIRED at T-P0-084h -- producer moved, not re-measured	purpose=timing
# ★★★★★ T-P0-054 AC-3: p3b WAS THE ONE PROBE THIS FILE DID NOT LIST, and it is the integration
# probe -- 48,537 bytes of source and sixteen p3_* routines built by no gate at all. Every defect
# of the last four tasks lived here (p3_clear_planes' 2-byte clear, the shadow buffer, the byte in
# the instruction stream), which is precisely the code the eight rows above never assembled.
# ★★★★ THE FLAGS WERE RECOVERED BY BYTE-MATCH, not from memory: this line reproduces the shipped
# build/p3b_probe_pk_fresh.bin at 12,859 bytes IDENTICAL. Six other plausible flag sets were tried
# ★★★★ THE 12,859 IS T-P0-054's AND IS NOW HISTORY, NOT A CHECK. P6.4 wired the parser into this
# probe: the image is **13,890 bytes** = 13,020 of code ($2000..P3_CODE_END $52DC) + 870 of
# src/engine/parser.s, which is `org`'d to $E000 and poked as a SECOND SEGMENT [idiom 43d].
# ★★★ So the byte-match that RECOVERED this row's flags cannot be repeated against 12,859, and a
# reader who tries it will conclude the flag set is wrong. The flags are unchanged and are still
# the row below; the size moved because the program did. **A recorded number whose producer has
# changed is the defect this file exists to prevent** [AD-95, and the cel gate's 6,782 fossil].
# ★★ To re-derive the flags today, byte-match against 13,890 with the parser included.
# and none did.
# ★★★★★ AND THE ROW LOOKS WRONG UNTIL YOU KNOW WHY. **PLANE_WIN_MMU is absent from this line and
# p3b IS windowed through the MMU**: `PLANE_WIN_MMU equ 1` is set UNCONDITIONALLY IN THE SOURCE
# [p3b_probe.s:65], so passing it on the command line is a Multiply-defined-symbol error and every
# build that tries FAILS TO ASSEMBLE. ★★★ Do not "fix" this row by adding it. The reading it
# invites -- "no PLANE_WIN_MMU, so p3b does not window" -- is the exact inverse of the truth, and
# is the same inert-flag confusion that made three of P3b.15/16's results meaningless [AD-119].
# ★★ Contrast the pic_win row above, which passes -DPLANE_WINDOWED and NOT -DPLANE_WIN_MMU and
# therefore genuinely does NOT window: the same two symbols mean opposite things in the two files.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ★★★★★ THIS ROW'S BINARY IS RE-BASELINED AT T-P0-084h, AND THE OLD IDENTITY IS RETIRED, NOT LOST.
#     retired:  F51FF8482D0B07E49F46B18612D20B06  13,925 B   (valid to P6.28g)
#     current:  58AD3C27164BD63FDE17E18041160B28  13,918 B
# ★★★★ WHY IT MOVED: the LOGIC decode landed at vm_bind_logic [vm_run.s], and p3b links it. It got
# 7 bytes SMALLER on balance -- the decode costs 7 and T-P0-084g/h removed p3_zero_timers, 14 bytes
# of dead code this file's own header had described as dead since P3b.1.
# ★★★ A reader who meets F51FF848 in P6.28b-g is looking at a RETIRED baseline, not a broken build.
# That distinction is why the old value stays written down [§2F: one home, including for the thing
# that is no longer true].
# ★★ THE FLAGS AND THE PURPOSE ARE UNCHANGED, so this is NOT AD-96's shape: the row still builds
# the same program under the same flags, and it carries no median in column 5 to invalidate.
p3b	src/harness/p3b_probe.s	build/p3b_probe_pk_fresh.bin	-DHAL_GFX_MODE_SERVICE -DHAL_SYS_FAST_CLOCK -DPLANE_WINDOWED -DPRI_PACKED	integration probe -- PLANE_WIN_MMU comes from the SOURCE (line 65), never the command line; binary 58AD3C27 13,918 B, re-baselined T-P0-084h	purpose=timing
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ★★★★★ p3b_text -- THE SAME SOURCE, A SECOND CONFIGURATION [ruling C, T-P0-084f].
#
# ★★★★★ IT IS A NEW ROW RATHER THAN AN EDIT TO THE ONE ABOVE, AND THIS FILE IS WHY. The decode fix
# (res_decode on the LOGIC cache-miss path) costs THREE BYTES, and the `p3b` row's cel
# configuration had ONE byte of headroom against CP_CEL -- so it landed 2 over and the collision
# guard refused the build. **Re-pointing the row above would have made everything green and
# invalidated every published p3b timing figure**, which is this file's own header ("Flags are
# load-bearing ... is a different program") and AD-96 recorded in the file that would have been
# edited. The timing binary keeps its identity: F51FF8482D0B07E49F46B18612D20B06, 13,925 B.
#
# ★★★★ WHAT THIS ROW BUILDS: -DP3B_NO_CEL strips view_cel.s and composite.s [ruling A, AD-180], so
# MAP_RESERVED is free for src/engine/text.s and the nine text opcodes.
# ★★★★★ AND IT RENDERS READABLE TEXT AS OF T-P0-084h. The LOGIC decode is at vm_bind_logic on a
# fresh open -- where the oracle puts it [agi.cpp:489-500, logic.cpp:56 at 9d9b9e93] -- so a
# LOGIC's messages reach the renderer as text rather than ciphertext. Jay, on the eye gate: "the
# text appreaed was readable and stayed in the sroll box" [AD-187]; the fault arm, all nine opcodes
# aliased back to vm_op_modelled, showed a black panel [AD-185].
# ★★★ Held OUT of run_gates.sh for two tasks, deliberately: until the decode landed this row would
# have gated HEALTH over a ciphertext build -- green for the wrong reason. It is in the suite now.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ★★★★★ RE-BASELINED AT T-P0-085c, AND THE OLD IDENTITY IS RETIRED, NOT LOST [AD-96].
#     retired:  FA7F2FB9...  14,582 B   (valid to P6.29b)
#     now:      AF0B2A027A960DF4...  15,036 B
# ★★★★ THE FLAG SET GAINED -DHAL_KEYBOARD, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE REASON THE ROW MOVED. print now
# BLOCKS until ENTER or ESC [T-P0-085c], so this configuration must link the key decoder; it did
# not link ANY key input before, in either configuration. ~318 B [P6.24] plus 148 B of wait loop,
# out of 624 bytes of headroom -- P3_CODE_END $5590 -> $5756, leaving 170 B to P3_FONT $5800.
# ★★★★★ -DHAL_KEYBOARD SELECTS EXISTING HAL CODE AND IS NOT A HAL CHANGE. hal_sync_check.py is
# clean on all three siblings; no shared file was touched [§2M].
# ★★★★★ `p3b` IS UNTOUCHED AND WAS VERIFIED SO, NOT ASSUMED: it reassembles to 58AD3C27... at
# 13,918 B, byte-identical, with P3_CODE_END still $52F8 and 8 bytes of spare against CP_CEL
# $5300. The nine `equ vm_op_modelled` aliases emit no bytes, which is what keeps that true.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ★★★★★ RE-BASELINED AGAIN AT T-P0-087+ (Jay: "do it"), AND THE FLAG SET GAINED -DP3B_IRQ.
#     retired:  AF0B2A027A960DF4...  15,036 B   (valid P6.29c..P6.31)
#     then:     9D2F925F03D21B2E...  15,052 B   (valid to the message-box work)
#     then:     ED3F248A0ACC9B0A...  15,548 B   -- box drawn, restore scoped, 128-glyph font
#     now:      63597E4DE0AB58EF...  15,561 B   -- T-P0-088: the restore copies its full width
# ★★★★★ WHY: print's wait loop paces off hal_frame, and NO PROBE HAS EVER ADVANCED IT. The CoCo3
# redirects the 6809 vectors into the $FExx page, so the chain is TWO hops -- $FFF8 -> $FEF7
# (LBRA, wrapping to $010C) -> $010C (JMP handler) -- and HAL_time_init patches only the second.
# This probe's MMU remap destroys the first, measured with IRQs still masked [a07895e]. So the
# text configuration installs its own JMP at $FEF7 and reserves $FEF0-$FF00 out of the vocabulary
# window. **Without interrupts this row cannot run the code it exists to test.**
# ★★★★ EVERY TEXT ARM CARRIES -DP3B_IRQ, so each fault arm differs from the clean arm by exactly
# one variable [L-73]. -NoIrq turns it off and is how the IRQs-off hang stays reproducible [§2W].
# ★★★ `p3b` is UNTOUCHED and verified so: 58AD3C27..., 13,918 B, spare 8. That row is
# purpose=timing and an interrupt every 16.667 ms would move every figure in it.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ★★★★★ WHAT THIS ROW STILL CANNOT GATE -- CORRECTED, AND THE CORRECTION IS SMALLER THAN IT LOOKS
# [was: "the wait loop is dead code under this corpus", T-P0-085c §7].
# ★★★★ The wait loop is no longer dead: it runs, holds and auto-closes, and its fault arm goes red
# [p3b_notick, below]. **But THIS ROW still does not reach it.** It runs Kingquest1 at room 83, and
# no title in the pinned set executes print from its intro:
#   - vm_opcov.py: $65/$66 in the NEVER-REACHED list for all nine titles at 600 cycles
#   - print_first_cycle.py: nine titles, 3,000 cycles, no input -- print NEVER executes
#   - vm_input_script.py --wants-print: six titles, every synthesisable said() line -- zero reach it
# ★★★★★ REACHING IT NEEDS A ROOM JUMP, WHICH IS A DIFFERENT ROW, NOT A FLAG: SpaceQuest-2 room 101
# with P3B_ROOM/P3B_SETVAR/P3B_VAR21 [p3b_box, below]. **A green run of THIS row says the wired
# opcodes, the decode and the text engine still work, and says nothing about the blocking window.**
# ★★★ Kept as a separate statement rather than folded away, because the flag changing and the
# coverage changing are different facts and only one of them happened here [L-86].
# ★★★ Room 83 stages ZERO sprites, so nothing is lost by stripping the compositing path HERE --
# and that is scoped to this row, not a claim about the engine.
# ★★ purpose=correctness: this row is gated on health and on what a person sees, not on a clock.
# **No timing figure may be quoted from it** -- the row above is the timing build.
p3b_text	src/harness/p3b_probe.s	build/p3b_probe_text.bin	-DHAL_GFX_MODE_SERVICE -DHAL_SYS_FAST_CLOCK -DPLANE_WINDOWED -DPRI_PACKED -DP3B_NO_CEL -DHAL_KEYBOARD -DP3B_IRQ	correctness probe: text opcodes, no cel staging, room 83; binary 63597E4D 15,561 B, re-baselined T-P0-088	purpose=correctness
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ★★★★★ THE FAULT ARM, AND IT HAS NOW BEEN SEEN RED. Blocked for three tasks; §2W is satisfied.
#     retired:  2268DAB7...  15,033 B   (built but unexercisable, P6.29c..P6.31)
#     then:     EEBA4C73...  15,049 B
#     then:     ED500A37...  15,545 B
#     now:      DA798353...  15,558 B   -- T-P0-088
# ★★★★ -DTEXT_FAULT_NOTICK drops ONE `jsr vm_step_clock` from print's wait loop -- 3 bytes, and
# nothing else differs from the row above. var 21's deadline is a mark ON the game clock, so a loop
# that does not advance that clock can never reach it.
# ★★★★★ MEASURED, under the p3b_box trigger below:
#     clean  40 cycles, no stall; box held 66 ticks (1.10 s) against var21=2's 60, then closed
#     fault  STUCK in cycle 9, watchdog fires at 1800 frames
#     and the discrimination is clean: hal_frame advances +1799 in BOTH arms while vm_vms advances
#     +66 clean and +0 fault. **Interrupts stay healthy and only the game clock is starved**, which
#     is exactly the defect the §4A census named rather than a hang arranged by some other route.
# ★★★ NOT in run_gates.sh: a fault arm belongs beside its gate, not inside the green path.
p3b_notick	src/harness/p3b_probe.s	build/p3b_probe_notick.bin	-DHAL_GFX_MODE_SERVICE -DHAL_SYS_FAST_CLOCK -DPLANE_WINDOWED -DPRI_PACKED -DP3B_NO_CEL -DHAL_KEYBOARD -DP3B_IRQ -DTEXT_FAULT_NOTICK	fault arm for print's wait loop -- shown RED T-P0-087+; see above	purpose=fault
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ★★★★★ p3b_box -- THE ROW THAT ACTUALLY GATES THE BLOCKING WINDOW. Same binary as p3b_text; what
# differs is the TRIGGER, and the trigger is the part that was missing for four tasks.
# ★★★★ IT IS THE ENVIRONMENT, NOT THE FLAGS, AND THAT IS WHY IT IS A ROW. §2F says the scope and
# the invocation of a gate are part of its definition; this project has recorded that five times
# (res 74-vs-1,264, cel 1-title-vs-6, pic without picgate, the VM's nine titles in an env var, and
# p3b itself). A second row with the same flags and a different corpus is the honest shape.
#     P3B_TITLE=SpaceQuest-2  P3B_ROOM=101  P3B_ROOM_AT=8  P3B_SETVAR=17=1  P3B_VAR21=2
# ★★★ WHY THIS ROOM, MEASURED NOT CHOSEN [P6.30 §4A/§4B]: logic 101 is `print.v(v17); quit(1)`,
# unconditional, has a PICTURE (so the integration probe can be IN it), does not halt the VM, and
# reaches print at cycle 8 identically across runs. var 17 must be set or the message number
# resolves to -1 and print draws nothing -- "the opcode executed" and "a box was drawn" are
# different facts [P6.31].
# ★★ Its determinism evidence and its two arms are in the block above.
# ★★★★★ IT IS IN run_gates.sh AS OF THIS CHANGE, AND THE REASON IT WAS HELD OUT WAS WRONG. The
# note here said the clean arm ends via quit(1) so the completion adjudicator would read it as a
# failure. **Measured: the probe keeps cycling after vm_quit, reaches its full count and exits 0.**
# The claim was never tested when it was written -- recorded rather than quietly deleted, because
# an untested reason for excluding a gate is how a gate stays excluded [§2W].
p3b_box	src/harness/p3b_probe.s	build/p3b_probe_text.bin	-DHAL_GFX_MODE_SERVICE -DHAL_SYS_FAST_CLOCK -DPLANE_WINDOWED -DPRI_PACKED -DP3B_NO_CEL -DHAL_KEYBOARD -DP3B_IRQ	blocking message window: SpaceQuest-2 room 101 via P3B_ROOM/P3B_SETVAR/P3B_VAR21; gates what p3b_text cannot	purpose=correctness
